{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02080",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.92,
      "end_seconds": 4.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I think it's my turn."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.0,
      "end_seconds": 13.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "Yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.05,
      "end_seconds": 30.84,
      "duration_seconds": 15.79,
      "text": "I've been getting out of breath, and I wanted to get it checked. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.54,
      "end_seconds": 35.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "How long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.38,
      "end_seconds": 44.54,
      "duration_seconds": 8.16,
      "text": "It's been about a month, I'm fairly sure. It's the not knowing that gets to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.1,
      "end_seconds": 49.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "How strong would you say it is?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.56,
      "end_seconds": 61.53,
      "duration_seconds": 10.97,
      "text": "So, pretty severe, if I'm being honest. And green phlegm lately, too. With green phlegm lately, I'd say mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.66,
      "end_seconds": 69.18,
      "duration_seconds": 6.52,
      "text": "What about a chronic cough with lots of phlegm, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.82,
      "end_seconds": 81.41,
      "duration_seconds": 10.59,
      "text": "Right, yes, for five days. So, uh, about chronic cough with lots of phlegm, honestly, all the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.38,
      "end_seconds": 99.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Have you had any coughing up blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.11,
      "end_seconds": 106.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.18,
      "text": "No, you know, I haven't had any coughing up blood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.39,
      "end_seconds": 113.43,
      "duration_seconds": 6.04,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any chest pain, fever or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.18,
      "end_seconds": 118.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.73,
      "text": "Let me think, no, I'd have said so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.44,
      "end_seconds": 123.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Anything on the skin I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.85,
      "end_seconds": 126.83,
      "duration_seconds": 0.98,
      "text": "No rashes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.56,
      "end_seconds": 131.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.0,
      "end_seconds": 135.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Bowels are regular, nothing odd."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.48,
      "end_seconds": 141.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.94,
      "end_seconds": 157.67,
      "duration_seconds": 14.73,
      "text": "It's iron tablets, once a day. So, it's hydrocortisone cream, when needed for the eczema. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.57,
      "end_seconds": 162.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.35,
      "end_seconds": 176.08,
      "duration_seconds": 12.73,
      "text": "I hardly move around during the day. I'm vegetarian and have been for years. My husband and I live above the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.97,
      "end_seconds": 179.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.3,
      "end_seconds": 186.59,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "I've had low haemoglobin for about a year now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.12,
      "end_seconds": 192.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "Is there anything more?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.66,
      "end_seconds": 194.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "Yes, eczema."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.68,
      "end_seconds": 198.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "So, anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.68,
      "end_seconds": 212.68,
      "duration_seconds": 9.0,
      "text": "Okay, I can see low haemoglobin and eczema in your file as well. I'll note down your vital signs first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.18,
      "end_seconds": 223.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.77,
      "end_seconds": 246.23,
      "duration_seconds": 10.46,
      "text": "Okay: pulse is 69 beats a minute, blood pressure 117 over 69, respiratory rate 17, SpO2 99 percent on room air."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.2,
      "end_seconds": 248.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.46,
      "end_seconds": 252.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "I'll come back to the numbers."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.37,
      "end_seconds": 257.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.24,
      "end_seconds": 261.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.54,
      "end_seconds": 276.13,
      "duration_seconds": 5.59,
      "text": "There are coarse crackles at both bases and the fingers are slightly clubbed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.85,
      "end_seconds": 282.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "You can sit up now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.71,
      "end_seconds": 332.64,
      "duration_seconds": 36.93,
      "text": "Taking everything into account, this is probably a flare of bronchiectasis. Another possibility is a chest infection. A chest X-ray is what I'd like next, for bronchiectasis flare. A sputum culture is what I'd like next, for purulent sputum. I'll start you on clarithromycin, 500 milligrams, twice a day, fourteen days. It's for bronchiectasis flare. Keep up your airway clearance exercises twice a day. Let's get you seen by the respiratory clinic, I'll arrange the letter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 334.21,
      "end_seconds": 338.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "Alright, what are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 340.4,
      "end_seconds": 347.15,
      "duration_seconds": 6.75,
      "text": "So, I take the clarithromycin, 500 milligrams, twice a day. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.33,
      "end_seconds": 352.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 353.88,
      "end_seconds": 356.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}